  "limitations": [
    "Union of first spaced eligible states per gate, capped per period, on legacy trajectories.",
    "Each alternative passes every original gate except exactly one positional heuristic.",
    "Counterfactual forces that pass for one decision, including over original shot priority.",
    "Fresh B edge, original cue/recipient executor; subsequent decisions use Classic.",
    "Attack credit stops at four consecutive opponent or stopped-clock frames; continuation runs to horizon, period end or first goal.",
    "Counterattack goals conceded count even after losing the initial attack.",
    "Cases can overlap and are correlated; split complete seeds and both assignments together.",
    "The shooting-window and comparative-position filters are tested separately. A pass failing both is not admitted.",
    "Existing geometric/risk checks are forecasts, not guarantees of native reception or correct recipient selection.",
    "The two fixed controls choose the highest original shot-value/margin candidate within a gate, then force it once; unaffected states retain Classic.",
    "Forcing a diagnostic pass can also change the original normal-shot priority; these results are not a pure remove-a-gate gameplay toggle.",
    "Native original-receiver one-timer attribution requires the initial commitment and intended shooter. Another recipient firing is not success for that intended opportunity.",
    "Training used 26101\u201326120; validation 26401\u201326410. Both team assignments and every alternative from a seed stay together.",
    "Thresholds use training unique-feature quartiles, with 0.5 for binary features. The threshold search can overfit correlated cases.",
    "At least 20 affected cases, five seeds and three net attack-return gains were required before validation. The best supported training rule gained only two.",
    "Validation did not choose a replacement rule, and thresholds were not relaxed after results were known.",
